course: dictionary
lesson: 6402
title: Words for a flock in the sky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a whole group doing one thing together. Look at the words around the new word to find its meaning. «A huge swirling cloud of starlings at dusk is called a murmuration.» The clues are huge, swirling, cloud and starlings, so a murmuration is a big group of birds moving together.
explain: Words can have more than one meaning. Murmuration also has a literary meaning: a soft, low murmuring sound, like a quiet hum. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning fits.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Tens of thousands of starlings fly together before roosting in shapes called murmurations.» If you put flock in place of murmurations and the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is probably right.
fact: A murmuration is a huge flock of starlings flying together.
fact: «Murmuration» means a huge swirling flock of starlings, usually at dusk.
fact: Flying together keeps starlings safer from hawks and falcons.
fact: Each bird watches about 7 of its nearest neighbours and copies them, so the whole flock moves like smoke.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, murmurations are watched in autumn and winter.
exercise: «A huge swirling cloud of starlings at dusk is called a murmuration.» What is a murmuration? | A small nest of baby birds | A sunny day at the beach | *A huge flock of starlings flying together
exercise: «A murmuration of starlings» flies together to keep safer from hawks. Why do they fly together? | To make a loud noise | To keep warm in the sun | To find food under the sea | *To stay safer from hawks
exercise: «Each bird watches only its nearest neighbours.» Find and copy one word that means the closest birds. | watches | *neighbours | swirling | dusk
test: «Each bird watches about 7 nearest neighbours.» What does each bird watch? | The falcon | *Its 7 nearest neighbours | The clouds at dusk | The sun
test: «The soft murmuration of the wind moved through the trees.» What does murmuration mean here? | *A soft, low murmuring sound | Huge flock of birds | A cloud of rain | A loud shout
exam: Jayden says murmuration is only a word for birds. Why is he only partly right? | It is only used in summer | It only means a hawk | It means a sunny day | *It can also mean a soft, low murmuring sound
